{
  "about": "The stage show: the songs and their performers. fair.config.json points here (fairWorld.audio.stage.songsFile). SONGS, in playlist order. Each has a timeline per part of the show, in seconds from the song's start, an entry where it changes: lute, drum and flute [second, rest | normal | fast | away] (whoever plays that instrument follows it: rest holds it, still; fast plays its loop faster, by FAST's speed; away puts it away), singers [second, sing | rest] (singing, they make the 'sing' moves, the Civil War cheer; resting, their lines are skipped and they make the 'rest' moves, clapping) and crowd [second, dance | clap | cheer]. Before a timeline's first entry, the instruments play, the singers sing and the crowd dances. Keep each timeline in order. tools/bards/build_sections.py --force re-seeds a song's timelines from its stems (overwriting your edits). INSTRUMENTS: names for the idles and forms below. FAST: how many times faster each instrument's loop plays in a 'fast' stretch (tools/bards/build_tempo.py makes the clips). BAND and ORCHESTRA: 'idle' is the instrument (an instruments name, or an idle's FormID); 'at' is [x, y, height, facing]. CROWD MOVES: the idles the dancers play in a dance, clap or cheer stretch, each with its clip length in seconds (vanilla idles play once; the stage script replays each as it ends). The cheer moves also play once at every song's end. SINGER MOVES: the singers' gestures while they sing, while they rest (a 'rest' stretch in their timeline), and the one they make at a song's end ('end'), with clip lengths; SINGER GAP is the seconds each stands between moves. SINGER STEPS: while they sing, the three step sideways across the deck as a line, facing the crowd: 'offsets' in turn (units; plus is east, to the crowd's right), one every 'every' seconds, the first where each song starts; 'stepSeconds' is how long a step takes (no gesture starts during one); resting, they go back to their marks. An empty 'offsets' keeps them still. 'names' are labels only. Rebuild after editing. MORE DANCES: when Professional Dancer (Nexus 124608) is loaded (moreDancesPlugin; install it and run Pandora so its dances exist), the dancers take these in turn while dancing (its animation events, and each clip's length in seconds); otherwise the vanilla dances. FIREWORKS, the fair's own (vanilla effects, no dependency, no damage): as each song ends, the afterSong shells go up from the sites, one per site in turn, 'stagger' seconds apart; at night (20:00-05:00) the atNight ones too, from the middle site. Shells: gold, blue, violet; 'climb' is the seconds each climbs before it bursts (1,500 units a second). set SkyrimFairFireworks to 0 to stop them.",
